WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
In 1290, King Edward the First
expelled every Jew from England.

2
00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.480
In 1656, Jews were allowed back.

3
00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.380
In 1701 they built Bevis
Marks synagogue in London.

4
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:13.960
It is still in use.

5
00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.840
Later came refugees from Russian pogroms,

6
00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.340
then children escaping the Nazis.

7
00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:24.580
So how have Jews in Britain
stayed Jewish for over 350 years,

8
00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.460
without hiding or
shutting themselves away?

9
00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:32.500
In this mission, you'll read a letter
sent long ago to Jewish exiles in Babylon,

10
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.040
telling them how to live far from home.

11
00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:39.470
Then you'll meet one British Jewish family
and decide which description fits them

12
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.440
best.

13
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:45.570
Your mission: explain how Jews in Britain
have stayed Jewish without hiding or

14
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.070
shutting themselves away.
